{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdKFFzs7MxiKXjdcrqzS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because a decimal number reached DynamoDB as a Python float, which boto3 refuses. I've fixed it so every write converts floats first, and written the cause and fix to `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why only the second publish:** each story is stored with its three most similar stories and a similarity score for each. That score is a float, and boto3 throws `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` On the first publish the library was empty, so there was nothing to score and no float in the item. From the second publish on there's always a float, so `put_item` throws and the handler returns 500.\n\n**The fix, so it can't come back:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` converts every float in the item to `Decimal`, at any depth. `publish()` runs the whole item through it just before writing. Because this covers the whole item rather than just the score field, a float added to the item later won't cause the same failure.\n- **`tests/fake_dynamo.py`:** the in-memory test table now returns every number as `Decimal`, as real DynamoDB does. Before, it handed back plain numbers, so it was more forgiving than production.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** one new test publishes three stories through the request handler and expects 201 each time; another checks the float conversion. The old test only ever published into an empty table, the one case where the bug can't happen.\n\nThe tests pass (3 OK). With the fix in `src/app.py` reverted, the new test fails with the same `TypeError` as the production log, so it catches this exact bug. Production will accept publishes again once you run `sam deploy`; I didn't deploy anything.\n\nWorklore suggested three stories; one (\"My tests passed because they agreed with me\") is why I made the test table behave like real DynamoDB. I didn't record a reproduction for it with worklore, because your rules say not to report to external services.\n\n**Separately:** `README.md` and `samconfig.toml` contain what look like real API credentials in plain text. Consider rotating them and moving them out of the repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":31206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d337989-8bef-4930-bd7c-7b93fdbcc051","uuid":"488252cf-9834-414e-839b-85bcf72030bb","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:30:40.742Z","request_id":"req_011CgdKFFijsCSAgefjZLUwg"}
